else-as-a-statement\n\nThe fix is a little weird, because the existing rule wants to treat `if (x) var y = 1` as a single statement, when _technically_ it's two. But I think I get the general feeling behind this.\n\nOn a similar note, the current tests don't have any examples of `return`, but I was thinking it might be nice to treat a function body that only has 1 statement as an expression, so the following would be allowed:\n\n``` js\nreturn function(x) { return x * 1; };\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/213936189/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"glenjamin","id":151272,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151272?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin","html_url":"https://github.com/glenjamin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/glenjamin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/213991996","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/5926#issuecomment-213991996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/5926","id":213991996,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxMz